  "decision_conditions": [
    "The first floor flat, due to an undersized gross internal area, would not achieve an acceptable standard of accommodation, in terms of sense of space, ventilation and cooling, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM10 of Kingston's Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient evidence, in the form of a daylight/sunlight assessment or assessment against the BRE 45 and 25 degree test, has been submitted to determine if the proposal would not result in unacceptable impacts on the residential amenity of the upper floor neighbours at no. 21 High Street, in terms of their access to daylight and sunlight, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM10 of Kingston's Core Strategy 2012. \r\r",
    "Insufficient information, in the form of a parking survey, has been submitted to demonstrate the additional uplift in on-street parking demand from the development would not result in unacceptable impacts on the local highway, contrary to Paragraph 116 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2021, Policy T6 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM9 of Kingston's Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The proposed refuse and cycle storage facilities are located outside the red line boundary. Insufficient evidence has been submitted to demonstrate these facilities can reasonably be provided to encourage residents to use sustainable transport modes and efficiently store waste for collection, contrary to Policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM10 of Kingston's Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
